Files: Cargo.lock
Copyright: 2026 Boswas Group
License: LicenseRef-Boswas-Internal
Comment: This file pins the Rust crates the build downloads from crates.io.
 boswas-compositor and boswas-shell are linked statically with those crates
 and with the Rust standard library. Each crate is copyright its authors and
 is used under the licence it is published with; "cargo tree --locked
 --format '{p} {l}'" in this directory prints the complete list. The main
 ones:
 .
  * Smithay and smithay-client-toolkit (the Smithay project), calloop,
    wayland-rs, drm-rs, gbm.rs, input.rs, pixman-rs: MIT
  * tiny-skia (Yevhenii Reizner): BSD-3-Clause; resvg and usvg: MIT or
    Apache-2.0
  * cosmic-text (System76): MIT or Apache-2.0; rustybuzz, ttf-parser,
    fontdb, swash, zeno: MIT or Apache-2.0 (and Zlib for parts)
  * winit: Apache-2.0; image, png: MIT or Apache-2.0
  * serde, serde_json, toml, chrono, rustix, libc, bitflags, tracing,
    zeroize, xkbcommon-rs, xcursor: MIT or Apache-2.0
  * zbus and its zvariant and zbus_names crates (the D-Bus library of the
    services): MIT; async-io, async-channel, async-executor, futures-lite
    and the other smol crates they build on: MIT or Apache-2.0; x11rb
    (X11 window management for Xwayland): MIT or Apache-2.0
  * unicode data crates: Unicode-3.0 (alongside MIT or Apache-2.0)
 .
 The licence texts are in the crates' sources and, for the licences Debian
 ships, in /usr/share/common-licenses.

Files: crates/boswas-shell/data/emoji.tsv
Copyright: 1991-2023 Unicode, Inc.
License: Unicode-3.0
Comment: The emoji panel's names, keywords, groups and skin tones, selected
 and reformatted by tools/build_emoji.py from Unicode's emoji-test.txt,
 UnicodeData.txt and CLDR's English annotations (Debian's unicode-data and
 unicode-cldr-core). The kaomoji and the choice of symbols in the file are
 Boswas's own. The shell embeds the file. See crates/boswas-shell/data/README.

